W22-WB-D + W22-WB-F operator iters confirmed PAUSE-Quit hard locks
the system on both real Vibra16S CT2490 AND DOSBox-X 2025.02. Engine
reaches `Script engine shutdown` then `snd-shutdown[4/6]: pre-MIX_
DestroyMixer` then never returns. Cross-platform reproduction means
DOSBox-X smoke can be relied on for fix validation here.

Root cause (localized via transient bracket logging through
MIX_DestroyMixer → SDL_DestroyAudioStream → SDL_CloseAudioDevice →
ClosePhysicalAudioDevice → SDL_WaitThread):

The audio playback thread (PlaybackAudioThread, created in
vendor/SDL/src/audio/SDL_audio.c:1887) is stuck inside
DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice's infinite for-loop waiting for ring
buffer drain. With force-pause active (SDL/0040 issues DSP 0xD5
at OpenDevice), the DSP is paused → DMA halted → IRQ-5 stops
firing → ring buffer never drains → the thread spins forever
yielding to main.

Main thread (in ClosePhysicalAudioDevice) sets device->shutdown=1
and calls SDL_WaitThread to join the audio thread. SDL_WaitThread
on DOS calls DOS_JoinThread which BLOCKS the main thread waiting
for the audio thread to finish. The cooperative scheduler keeps
yielding back and forth: audio thread spins in WaitDevice (no
shutdown check), main thread spins in DOS_JoinThread. Deadlock.

Fix: add a single shutdown check at the top of DOSSOUNDBLASTER_
WaitDevice's for-loop. When device->shutdown is set, return true
unconditionally. The calling SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate's
next iteration observes device->shutdown and exits the loop
cleanly (SDL_audio.c:1181), releasing the SDL_WaitThread join.

Why return true (not false): SDL_audio.c:1322 treats !WaitDevice
as a disconnect signal (SDL_AudioDeviceDisconnected fires). We
don't want to fire that on a clean shutdown. Returning true lets
the loop continue to the next SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate call,
which then sees shutdown=1 and exits via the normal path. The
intervening "fill ring with audio data" work is skipped because
that's gated on !shutdown inside Iterate.

This bug was masked at run-time on the organya path because the
DSP isn't paused — IRQ-5 fires, ring drains, WaitDevice returns
naturally on its own success condition. Only the force-pause
path (where IRQ-5 stops firing) hits the deadlock. Same on
DOSBox-X (which faithfully emulates the SB16 0xD5 pause command
and therefore reproduces the deadlock).

Performance impact: zero. SDL_GetAtomicInt is a single x86 load
of a volatile int — sub-µs on PODP83. Adds one cheap branch per
WaitDevice loop iteration, dominated by the existing DOS_Yield
+ MaybeServiceIdlePauseRequests calls.

Fixes:
  - W22-WB-D PAUSE.LOG / PAUSESDL.LOG hang at snd-shutdown[4/6]
  - W22-WB-F PAUSE.LOG / PAUSESDL.LOG same hang
  - Future force-pause-style measurement iters (any pause-DSP
    + clean-quit pattern)

Validation: DOSBox-X smoke reproduces the bug + the fix. Smoke
matrix: organya regression PASS (1s clean exit, full snd-shutdown
[1/6 .. 6/6] trace). Force-pause PASS (1s clean exit, full
snd-shutdown trace + SDL/0043 hard-reset path runs cleanly).
Per memory dosbox_not_behavioral_proxy_for_io.md, this is the
documented exception where DOSBox-X DOES faithfully reproduce
the IO behavior — fix validation here transfers to real HW.

Modifies vendor/SDL/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c only; no new
files; no new env vars; no doc changes required.
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 4d4eb510f..a9430c662 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -384,6 +384,21 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
     const int size = hidden->ring_size;
 
     for (;;) {
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0046): bail out early when the
+           audio device is shutting down. SDL3 audio core sets
+           device->shutdown=1 before calling SDL_WaitThread to join the
+           playback thread. If we're stuck spinning here (e.g., DSP is
+           force-paused via SDL/0040 → DMA halted → IRQ-5 stops firing
+           → ring buffer never drains), we'd deadlock with the main
+           thread — main waits for us to finish; we wait for ring to
+           drain that the IRQ that's not firing. Returning true on
+           shutdown lets the calling SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate's
+           next iteration observe device->shutdown and exit cleanly,
+           releasing the SDL_WaitThread join. */
+        if (SDL_GetAtomicInt(&device->shutdown)) {
+            return true;
+        }
+
         /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0038): service pause/resume
            requests on each WaitDevice loop iteration. Pause requests
            come from the IRQ handler (consecutive-silent-IRQ threshold
